---
# Relaxed rules for unit tests. Inherits from the project root .clang-tidy
# but disables checks that conflict with the Qt Test idiom:
#
# * misc-use-internal-linkage / readability-convert-member-functions-to-static:
#   Q_OBJECT test classes and their slots are invoked by MOC at runtime.
#   They can't move into an anonymous namespace and can't be static —
#   MOC needs to find the class by name and the slots by signature.
# * readability-identifier-naming: test method names follow the Qt Test
#   convention (`scenarioName_expectedBehaviour`), which the project's
#   FunctionCase=camelBack rejects.
# * cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access:
#   tests operate on hand-built stub data, indexed access is intentional.
# * misc-const-correctness on QCoreApplication: exec() is non-const so
#   app must stay non-const — this triggers a false positive when exec()
#   isn't called in the same TU clang-tidy is analysing.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static,
  -readability-identifier-naming,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -misc-const-correctness
